syn_map:|        |       |     | etc.                                             |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Check the consistency of the parameters, and see  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | if you can ignore this message or you're using   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | different LEF file with wrong parameters.        |
syn_map:|PHYS-279|Warning|   16|Physical cell not defined in library.             |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Ensure that the proper library files are available|
syn_map:|        |       |     | and have been imported.                          |
syn_map:|PHYS-752|Info   |    2|Partition Based Synthesis execution skipped.      |
syn_map:|POPT-502|Warning|    4|Total power has skewed contributions from leakage |
syn_map:|        |       |     | and dynamic power.                               |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Dynamic power is typically calculated/specified   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | for some 'active period'. For combination of     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | leakage and dynamic power                        |
syn_map:|        |       |     | opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio must specify the    |
syn_map:|        |       |     | percentage of overall time for which the design  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | is not in the 'active period' but in 'idle mode',|
syn_map:|        |       |     | i.e. no dynamic power but only leakage power is  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | consumed. For a reasonable optimization across   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | dynamic and leakage power, leakage contribution  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | is expected to be above 5% and below 95%. A      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | contribution of less than 5% will result in      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | limited leakage optimization and contribution of |
syn_map:|        |       |     | more than 95% will result in limited dynamic     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | optimization. Adjust                             |
syn_map:|        |       |     | 'opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio' so that leakage   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | contribution comes to an intermediate value if   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | you intend both optimizations to occur.          |
syn_map:|SYNTH-4 |Info   |    1|Mapping.                                          |
syn_map:|TUI-32  |Warning|    1|This attribute will be obsolete in a next major   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | release.                                         |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Attribute, 'number_of_routing_layers' on root is  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | going to be obsoleted. Use root attribute        |
syn_map:|        |       |     | 'design_top_routing_layer' instead.              |
syn_map:|TUI-58  |Info   |  235|Removed object.                                   |
