syn_opt:|PA-7    |Info   |    4|Resetting power analysis results.                 |
syn_opt:|        |       |     |All computed switching activities are removed.    |
syn_opt:|PHYS-12 |Warning|    6|The variant range of wire parameters is too large.|
syn_opt:|        |       |     | An example of wire parameters are, a WIDTH for   |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | layer, PITCH for layer, MINSPACING for layers,   |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | etc.                                             |
syn_opt:|        |       |     |Check the consistency of the parameters, and see  |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | if you can ignore this message or you're using   |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | different LEF file with wrong parameters.        |
syn_opt:|PHYS-279|Warning|   24|Physical cell not defined in library.             |
syn_opt:|        |       |     |Ensure that the proper library files are available|
syn_opt:|        |       |     | and have been imported.                          |
syn_opt:|POPT-51 |Info   |    3|Could not declone clock-gating instances.         |
syn_opt:|        |       |     |The design should have 2 or more clock-gating     |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | instances for decloning.                         |
syn_opt:|POPT-502|Warning|    6|Total power has skewed contributions from leakage |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | and dynamic power.                               |
syn_opt:|        |       |     |Dynamic power is typically calculated/specified   |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | for some 'active period'. For combination of     |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | leakage and dynamic power                        |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio must specify the    |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | percentage of overall time for which the design  |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | is not in the 'active period' but in 'idle mode',|
syn_opt:|        |       |     | i.e. no dynamic power but only leakage power is  |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | consumed. For a reasonable optimization across   |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | dynamic and leakage power, leakage contribution  |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | is expected to be above 5% and below 95%. A      |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | contribution of less than 5% will result in      |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | limited leakage optimization and contribution of |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | more than 95% will result in limited dynamic     |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | optimization. Adjust                             |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | 'opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio' so that leakage   |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | contribution comes to an intermediate value if   |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | you intend both optimizations to occur.          |
syn_opt:|SYNTH-7 |Info   |    1|Incrementally optimizing.                         |
syn_opt:|SYNTH-33|Warning|    1|The selected flow setting will be removed in a    |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | future release.                                  |
syn_opt:|        |       |     |Contact Cadence support to understand current     |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | flows.                                           |
syn_opt:|TUI-32  |Warning|    1|This attribute will be obsolete in a next major   |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | release.                                         |
syn_opt:|        |       |     |Attribute, 'number_of_routing_layers' on root is  |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | going to be obsoleted. Use root attribute        |
syn_opt:|        |       |     | 'design_top_routing_layer' instead.              |
syn_opt:|TUI-58  |Info   |  352|Removed object.                                   |
syn_opt:---------------------------------------------------------------------------
syn_opt:Info    : Done incrementally optimizing. [SYNTH-8]
syn_opt:        : Done incrementally optimizing 'Core'.
syn_opt:      flow.cputime  flow.realtime  timing.setup.tns  timing.setup.wns  snapshot
syn_opt:UM:*                                                                   syn_opt
syn_opt:#@ End verbose flow_step synthesis.syn_opt.run_syn_opt
syn_opt:      flow.cputime  flow.realtime  timing.setup.tns  timing.setup.wns  snapshot
syn_opt:UM:              5              5                                      run_syn_opt
